er":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-07T22:59:06-07:00","id":162230,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/118737-high-wyrd-kiths?p=162224#post162224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Where can that be found?</div> </div> </div> </div>Equinox Road, page 15. At Wyrd 7, all Kiths evolve into a new form. The book provides examples for all the ones for the core, except Earthbones (weirdly). Which is rather annoying, because I have an Earthbones Elemental in my Changeling game who just hit Wyrd 7 and I don't expect any others to hit the same level, so literally the only Kith I have to deal with is the one that wasn't covered.<br /> <br /> Ah well. Earthbones at least is pretty easy. It's just the same evolution as Fireheart, and the other &quot;spend Glamour for dice&quot; powers. Instead of spending Glamour to get bonus dice on non-combat Strength rolls on a one-for-one basis, they can now spend them on a one-for-two basis.<br /> <br /> Although I did toy with it evolving to let the character spend Glamour on combat Strength rolls...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.